---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import { meshiiCaseStudy } from '../../data/case-studies';
import '../../styles/case-meshii.css';

const sectionLinks = [
    { href: '#architecture', label: 'Architecture' },
    { href: '#decisions', label: 'Decisions' },
    { href: '#boundaries', label: 'Boundaries' },
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout
    study={meshiiCaseStudy}
    sectionLinks={sectionLinks}
>
    <Fragment slot="intro">
        I designed the app and AWS service architecture for a private Meshii WiFi pilot and led three
        developers through delivery. The system combined device setup, network performance data and test
        rewards on Polygon Mumbai, with one app for web, iOS and Android.
    </Fragment>
    <dl slot="facts" class="facts">
        <div class="fact">
            <dt>
                Role
            </dt>
            <dd>
                Software Architect
            </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
            <dt>
                Delivery
            </dt>
            <dd>
                Private pilot
            </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
            <dt>
                App
            </dt>
            <dd>
                React Native / Expo
            </dd>
        </div>
        <div class="fact">
            <dt>
                Services and data
            </dt>
            <dd>
                AWS / PostgreSQL / Polygon testnet
            </dd>
        </div>
    </dl>
    <section class="section" id="architecture">
        <div class="section__inner">
            <p class="eyebrow">
                01 / System design
            </p>
            <h2>
                How the system worked
            </h2>
            <div class="diagram" role="img" aria-label="Meshii system architecture showing how the app, AWS services, device performance data and test rewards connected">
                <div class="lane">
                    <p class="lane__label">
                        App for web, iOS and Android
                    </p>
                    <div class="flow">
                        <div class="node">
                            Web / iOS / Android
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Built with Expo / React Native
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Login, data and maps: Auth0 / React Query / Mapbox
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="lane">
                    <p class="lane__label">
                        Application services
                    </p>
                    <div class="flow">
                        <div class="node">
                            Secure API access: API Gateway + JWT
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Business functions: AWS Lambda
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Application records: PostgreSQL / Prisma
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Network and device services: RADIUSdesk / AWS IoT
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="lane">
                    <p class="lane__label">
                        Device performance data
                    </p>
                    <div class="flow">
                        <div class="node">
                            Mesh node performance data
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Collection: AWS IoT rules / Kinesis
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Storage and triggers: S3 / EventBridge
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Database and reward scoring: PostgreSQL
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="lane">
                    <p class="lane__label">
                        Test reward processing
                    </p>
                    <div class="flow">
                        <div class="node">
                            Calculated reward group
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Reward processing: AWS Lambda
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Test transaction: Alchemy / Polygon Mumbai
                        </div>
                        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">
                            -&gt;
                        </span>
                        <div class="node">
                            Signed notification / status update
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <p class="caption">
                I kept the application APIs separate from device-data processing. The APIs handled accounts,
                wallets, device pairing and configuration. Another set of services collected node
                measurements and calculated reward scores.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="decisions">
        <div class="section__inner">
            <p class="eyebrow">
                02 / Design decisions
            </p>
            <h2>
                Why I built it this way
            </h2>
            <div class="cards">
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        One app across three platforms
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        Expo and React Native let us share screens, navigation and API connections across
                        web, iOS and Android. Platform-specific code handled Auth0, Mapbox and nearby device
                        discovery through mDNS.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Bringing different data sources together
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        The app needed account information from cloud services, details from nearby devices
                        and blockchain transaction data. React Query gave the rest of the app a consistent
                        way to use those sources.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Application APIs and records
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        API Gateway, Lambda and shared code separated the services for users, wallets,
                        devices and maps. PostgreSQL and Prisma held the application's main records.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Device data as a separate workflow
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        AWS IoT rules, Kinesis, S3 and EventBridge handled device-data collection separately
                        from reward scoring and processing. That let us change each stage independently
                        during the pilot.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Test rewards on Polygon
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        Alchemy submitted groups of smart-contract reward transactions to Polygon Mumbai.
                        Signed notifications from Alchemy updated transaction status in the application
                        database.
                    </p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Builds and deployments
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        AWS SAM defined the services. GitHub Actions deployed changes using short-lived AWS
                        access through OIDC. Amplify hosted the Expo web app, and EAS configuration defined
                        preview builds for iOS and Android.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="boundaries">
        <div class="section__inner">
            <p class="eyebrow">
                03 / Beyond the pilot
            </p>
            <h2>
                What I'd finish before production
            </h2>
            <div class="boundary">
                <p>
                    This was a private pilot on Polygon Mumbai. The code records automated development and
                    staging deployments and unit tests with mocked dependencies. Before production, I would
                    need to test and harden the complete workflow: duplicate rewards, repeated events,
                    recovery during device setup and keeping blockchain transactions in sync with
                    application records. Native release automation would also need work.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div class="cards cards--spaced">
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Recovery and production controls
                    </h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Save a unique record for each reward group before submitting a blockchain
                            transaction.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Handle repeated events, retain failed events and regularly compare blockchain
                            transactions with application records.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Track recovery steps when device pairing spans multiple systems.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Limit each Lambda to the secrets and AWS permissions it needs.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>
                        Integration and release checks
                    </h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>
                            Test PostgreSQL, AWS SAM events and repeated webhook notifications together.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Check mDNS discovery, authentication and pairing on physical devices.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Bring development, staging and production infrastructure definitions into line.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Test deployment health and rollback after database changes.
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
    <section class="section">
        <div class="section__inner">
            <p class="eyebrow">
                04 / Source code and configuration
            </p>
            <h2>
                What I checked
            </h2>
            <ul class="evidence-list">
                <li>
                    Expo configuration, platform-specific connections, API code and component tests.
                </li>
                <li>
                    AWS SAM definitions for APIs, device-data processing, reward scoring and device setup.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Lambda code for authentication, device pairing, rewards and signed notifications.
                </li>
                <li>
                    Prisma and SQL changes for application records and device performance data.
                </li>
                <li>
                    GitHub Actions, Amplify and EAS build and deployment configuration.
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="caption">
                The source code is private. I've left out credentials, customer data, infrastructure
                and device identifiers, smart-contract addresses and private service addresses.
            </p>
            <div class="cta">
                <a class="button button--primary" href="/">
                    Back to portfolio
                </a>
                <a class="button" href="/Adam-Brewer-Senior-Full-Stack-Engineer-CV.pdf" download>
                    Download CV
                </a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>
